<speak>So your investment objective is to reduce your global equity exposure and free up cash for your planned personal commitments. For Summit Global Equity <sub alias="ee tee eff">ETF</sub>, falling global equity markets can reduce the value of its underlying holdings. When you sell, price movements or weaker trading liquidity can also mean you receive a less favourable price than the latest quote. Do you understand that falling equity markets can lower the holding's value, and that the actual sale price may be less favourable than the latest quote?</speak>